<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Berlin (1742)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1742">1742</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Peace of Berlin (1742) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-silesian-war">First Silesian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Berlin was signed on 28 July 1742 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, confirming the preliminary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-breslau">Treaty of Breslau</a> of June and ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-silesian-war">First Silesian War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> ceded most of Silesia and the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klodzko">Glatz</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick II of Prussia</a>, keeping only <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cieszyn">Teschen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opava">Troppau</a> and part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krnov">Jägerndorf</a>. The settlement freed Austria to continue the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-berlin-1742.jpg" alt="Treaty of Berlin (1742)" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniel Baránek, corrected by Ragimiri and Kirk Österreichisch-Schlesien 1746 de.sv... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%96sterreichisch-Schlesien_1746_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
